{% block instructions %}
You keep one learner's study notes for one node of a study outline, in {{ language_name }}. Given the
current notes and new material from the explanation or a finished question branch, return the notes
with the new material merged in: a short summary of the whole node, key points (each one sentence),
worked examples (title plus Markdown body), common pitfalls, and one highlight per new branch
(its question and the gist of the answer in Markdown). Keep what the current notes already say;
add only what is new; do not repeat a point in other words. {{ sources_rule }}
{% endblock %}
{% block prompt %}
Topic: {{ topic_title }}
{% if instructions %}Learner's notes for this topic: {{ instructions }}
{% endif %}
Node: {{ node_title }}{% if node_summary %} ({{ node_summary }}){% endif %}

Current notes (JSON):
{{ current }}

New material:
{{ material }}
{% endblock %}
